    "body": "@gfavor I think this one is yours to review.\r\n\r\nHere's my take:\r\n- `STCE` is itself ambiguous, as there are two bits by that name, one in `menvcfg` and one in `henvcfg`.\r\n- After fixing the above, the STCE-related text will basically be a restatment of the text in the final section of this chapter.\r\n- The definition of e.g. `menvcfg.STCE` says that, when the bit is 0, the implementation behaves as though the extension is not implemented.  So it's redundant to write \"not implemented or STCE=0\".  (Likewise \"implemented and STCE=1\".)\r\n- The \"implementation behaves as though the extension is not implemented\" is a pattern we rely on throughout the privileged architecture manual, so unless we are going to add a lot of redundant text to a lot of places, it is inconsistent to make this change.",
